#====================================================================
# E337 — 鸿蒙 file_manager 挂载点(hmdfs)不支持 Unix socket 创建
# 触发事件: herdr 0.8.2 HarmonyOS PC 适配（herdr server 默认路径启动失败）
#====================================================================

id:                     E337
trigger_tool:           runtime|server|test|install
phase:                  runtime
error_signature:        Operation not permitted|
                         PermissionDenied.*Operation not permitted|
                         failed to.*bind.*socket.*(Permission denied|Operation not permitted)|
                         Unable to create socket.*(Permission denied|Operation not permitted)|
                         Error: Os \{ code: 1, kind: PermissionDenied.*(socket|bind)

severity:               3
category:               ohos, hmdfs, socket, limitation, platform
match_keywords:         HarmonyOS, OHOS, hmdfs, file_manager, Unix socket, bind,
                         Operation not permitted, socket path, herdr, XDG_CONFIG_HOME,
                         XDG_STATE_HOME, daemon, IPC
title:                  HarmonyOS file_manager mount (hmdfs) cannot create Unix sockets

root_cause: >
  On HarmonyOS the user home (/storage/Users/currentUser) and its subdirectories such as
  ~/.config are served by the file_manager hmdfs mount. hmdfs does not support creating
  Unix domain sockets; a bind() attempt fails with EPERM ("Operation not permitted").
  Tools that create IPC/daemon sockets under the default config dir (e.g. herdr server
  creating herdr.sock under ~/.config/herdr) therefore fail at startup unless XDG_CONFIG_HOME
  / XDG_STATE_HOME (or the tool's socket path) points to a socket-capable directory such as
  an application data dir (/data/storage/el2/base/...).
affected_scope: >
  Any long-running service or daemon on HarmonyOS that binds a Unix socket under the user
  home / file_manager mount: herdr server (herdr.sock, herdr-client.sock), and similar
  IPC-based tools (tmux-style multiplexers, local HTTP/socket servers, language servers).
verification_cmd: >
  herdr server 2>&1 | grep -i "Operation not permitted"  (fails under default ~/.config/herdr);
  XDG_CONFIG_HOME=/data/storage/el2/base/files/home_dir/.config XDG_STATE_HOME=/data/storage/el2/base/files/home_dir/.state herdr server  (succeeds)

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           env-xdg-redirect
rec_description:        Set XDG_CONFIG_HOME/XDG_STATE_HOME to a socket-capable directory (e.g. app data dir) so the tool's sockets are created outside the file_manager mount.
rec_command:            export XDG_CONFIG_HOME=/data/storage/el2/base/files/home_dir/.config\n    export XDG_STATE_HOME=/data/storage/el2/base/files/home_dir/.state
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      tool-socket-flag
fallback_description:   If the tool exposes a socket path flag/env (e.g. HERDR_SOCKET_PATH), point it at a socket-capable directory instead of redirecting all XDG dirs.
fallback_command:       export HERDR_SOCKET_PATH=/data/storage/el2/base/cache/herdr.sock
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       chmod 777 .*|chown.*(socket|\.sock)|ln -sf.*\.sock
forbid_1_reason:        chmod/chown/symlink do not make hmdfs support socket creation; the mount itself rejects bind().
forbid_1_consequence:   Wasted debugging time; the underlying EPERM persists.

principles:             P-PLATFORM-001,P-LIMITATION-001

causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             E002,E046
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

